# 2026-07-06 git authentication maze

*Four separate walls in this session, in order:*
## What I was trying to do
==Trying to push to Github==
## What broke
1. `git add .` failed 
2. the push rejected my password
3. Tried to install the `gh` CLI but it didn't install
4. Push failed again
## What I thought was wrong
1. I thought that it was rejecting my folder 
2. I thought my password was wrong
3. I thought I had to reset my mac book
4. I thought that the whole thing was broken
## What was actually wrong
1. folder wasn't a repo yet because I never run `git init`
2. GitHub doesn't accept account passwords for git anymore.
3. `brew` wasn't installed
4. A Typo
## How I found it
1. When I ran the first command, the terminal shot back at me: "Not a git repository"
2. I ended up generating a Personal Access Token, and then pasted the token as the password.
3. I found the specific error when I went to troubleshoot online 
4. I put in `alex-sentinal` instead of `alex-sentinel`
## Takeaway
1. If git commands complain that the folder isn't a repo, it means I skipped `git init`
2. GitHub auth needs a token, not a password
3. My mac is fine, I have to check brew before assuming it's my setup 
4. check my username spelling
